WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.362
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.662 --> 00:00:09.199
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.499 --> 00:00:15.518
Unit twenty-one: Urban Resilience. Today you will recommend action using should + passive.

4
00:00:15.818 --> 00:00:18.471
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.433 --> 00:00:22.771
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:24.769
Resilience.

7
00:00:25.783 --> 00:00:29.803
Resilience means the ability of a city to absorb shocks and recover.

8
00:00:30.417 --> 00:00:32.741
Resilience was tested by the monsoon.

9
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:36.652
Your turn. Say: Resilience.

10
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:40.640
Resilience.

11
00:00:41.383 --> 00:00:42.164
Flooding.

12
00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:46.287
Flooding means the covering of normally dry land with water.

13
00:00:46.883 --> 00:00:49.254
Flooding closed the main road for three days.

14
00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:52.305
Your turn. Say: Flooding.

15
00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:55.947
Flooding.

16
00:00:56.683 --> 00:00:58.091
Infrastructure.

17
00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:03.358
Infrastructure means basic systems such as roads, drains and power.

18
00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.727
Ageing infrastructure failed under the storm.

19
00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:10.201
Your turn. Say: Infrastructure.

20
00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:14.358
Infrastructure.

21
00:01:15.117 --> 00:01:16.292
Adaptation.

22
00:01:17.283 --> 00:01:20.723
Adaptation means adjusting to expected climate effects.

23
00:01:21.317 --> 00:01:24.396
Adaptation includes raising homes above flood level.

24
00:01:24.983 --> 00:01:28.030
Your turn. Say: Adaptation.

25
00:01:30.867 --> 00:01:32.042
Adaptation.

26
00:01:32.783 --> 00:01:33.715
Heatwave.

27
00:01:34.717 --> 00:01:38.051
Heatwave means a long period of unusually hot weather.

28
00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:41.195
A heatwave strained the electricity grid.

29
00:01:41.783 --> 00:01:44.273
Your turn. Say: Heatwave.

30
00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:48.181
Heatwave.

31
00:01:48.917 --> 00:01:49.836
Planning.

32
00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:54.742
Planning means organising the use of land and resources in advance.

33
00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:57.802
Careful planning kept the new district dry.

34
00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:00.686
Your turn. Say: Planning.

35
00:02:03.533 --> 00:02:04.430
Planning.

36
00:02:05.183 --> 00:02:06.057
Community.

37
00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:10.222
Community means a group of people living in the same area.

38
00:02:10.817 --> 00:02:13.083
The community cleared the canals together.

39
00:02:13.683 --> 00:02:16.382
Your turn. Say: Community.

40
00:02:19.233 --> 00:02:20.200
Community.

41
00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:21.986
Recovery.

42
00:02:22.983 --> 00:02:26.864
Recovery means the return to normal conditions after a disaster.

43
00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:29.624
Recovery took months after the flood.

44
00:02:30.217 --> 00:02:32.857
Your turn. Say: Recovery.

45
00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:36.759
Recovery.

46
00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:41.635
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:42.483 --> 00:02:47.051
Visal, every rainy season parts of Phnom Penh flood. What should the city do?

48
00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:55.664
Drainage systems should be upgraded, and green spaces should be protected so that rainwater can be absorbed.

49
00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:58.204
Isn't that expensive?

50
00:02:59.317 --> 00:03:09.179
It is, but the costs of inaction are higher. Vulnerable neighbourhoods should be prioritised, and early warnings should be provided in every district.

51
00:03:10.283 --> 00:03:11.377
And residents?

52
00:03:12.483 --> 00:03:20.929
They should be involved in planning. Community knowledge must be used, and local volunteers should be trained for rapid recovery.

53
00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:23.915
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:28.514
Grammar focus: Should plus passive for recommendations.

55
00:03:28.814 --> 00:03:29.978
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:30.683 --> 00:03:34.064
Drainage systems should be upgraded before the next monsoon.

57
00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:37.936
Vulnerable neighbourhoods should be prioritised in the budget.

58
00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:41.082
Residents should be involved in planning.

59
00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:52.873
Recommend with should be + past participle: should be upgraded, should be protected. It is polite and impersonal because the actor is omitted. For strong need use must be + p.p.

60
00:03:53.617 --> 00:03:56.977
Be careful! Don't say: Drains should upgrade.

61
00:03:58.933 --> 00:04:01.316
Say: Drains should be upgraded.

62
00:04:01.616 --> 00:04:03.523
should be + past participle.

63
00:04:04.333 --> 00:04:06.812
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:09.309
A City That Bounces Back.

65
00:04:09.609 --> 00:04:15.045
Cities concentrate people and assets, so a single flood or heatwave can cause severe damage.

66
00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:20.436
Urban resilience is the capacity to absorb such shocks and recover quickly.

67
00:04:21.433 --> 00:04:28.843
Experts recommend that drainage systems should be upgraded, wetlands should be protected, and buildings should be designed for extreme heat.

68
00:04:29.833 --> 00:04:37.092
Vulnerable neighbourhoods should be prioritised, and residents should be involved in planning, since local knowledge is invaluable.

69
00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:42.758
Recovery plans must be prepared before disaster strikes, not afterwards.

70
00:04:43.867 --> 00:04:47.984
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:51.140
Drainage systems should blank upgraded.

72
00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:54.420
A, be. B, to be. C, been.

73
00:04:57.967 --> 00:04:59.630
The answer is A: be.

74
00:05:00.783 --> 00:05:03.979
The return to normal conditions after a disaster is blank.

75
00:05:04.279 --> 00:05:08.269
A, recovery. B, planning. C, heatwave.

76
00:05:11.833 --> 00:05:14.320
The answer is A: recovery.

77
00:05:15.483 --> 00:05:18.191
Basic systems such as roads and drains are blank.

78
00:05:18.491 --> 00:05:23.398
A, community. B, infrastructure. C, adaptation.

79
00:05:26.933 --> 00:05:29.351
The answer is B: infrastructure.

80
00:05:30.517 --> 00:05:32.296
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:32.596 --> 00:05:38.118
A, Wetlands should be protect.. B, Wetlands should be protected.. C, Wetlands should protected..

82
00:05:41.667 --> 00:05:44.607
The answer is B: Wetlands should be protected..

83
00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:49.398
According to the reading, recovery plans must be prepared…

84
00:05:49.698 --> 00:05:54.153
A, afterwards. B, before disaster strikes. C, never.

85
00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:00.686
The answer is B: before disaster strikes.

86
00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:05.179
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:06.017 --> 00:06:08.759
How could Phnom Penh become more resilient to flooding?

88
00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:27.190
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:51.333
Phnom Penh could become more resilient if drainage systems were upgraded, lakes and wetlands were protected, and new buildings were designed above flood levels. Early warnings should be provided to every district, and communities should be trained to respond. Planning must also protect vulnerable neighbourhoods, which suffer most.

90
00:06:51.633 --> 00:06:53.191
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:54.083 --> 00:06:59.139
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and should plus passive for recommendations.

92
00:06:59.439 --> 00:07:04.309
Today's value is community resilience. Stronger communities recover together.

93
00:07:04.609 --> 00:07:07.389
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

94
00:07:07.689 --> 00:07:10.399
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

